From 445998aaf063ecabb596793b436d3bc206da7502 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:44:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: expose typed database lifecycle and public
 obfuscation diagnostics

Convert all 11 node-owned dbwrapper producers with exact text, original levels,
categories and surrounding behavior. Keep file limits signed and the database
basename distinct from full paths. Existing XOR-obfuscation diagnostics use a
copied byte snapshot; this adds no wallet/private-key disclosure. Retain the
external LevelDB va_list/continuation forwarder with an explicit reviewed
infrastructure disposition, rather than parsing third-party prose into fields.

Add a focused real startup/mine/restart functional check for path types, key
stability and readable JSON diagnostics. Normal/native/functional gates remain
pending resource scheduling. AST fixtures16, lint contracts13, production lint
336 sites, Ruff0.15.8 and diff checks pass.

Scripted diff (ast-grep-py0.51.0, reviewed literal/typed-field mappings):
/private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/database-wrapper-lifecycle.json --report /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/logging-cleanup/database-wrapper-applied.json --apply
git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style '{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}' HEAD -- src/dbwrapper.cpp

Test, registry support and explicit disposition reviewed separately; the rule
catalog records all support adjustments and fails closed on changed input.

